  "content": {
    "title": "New Update: Tiger Woods Charged With DUI After Rollover Crash Near His Florida Home",
    "text": "Tiger Woods at the White House last year. — Official White House Photo by Molly RileyGolfing legend Tiger Woods was arrested in Florida on suspicion of DUI after a rollover crash on Jupiter Island, the latest troubling chapter in his history with vehicle-related incidents.The incident happened just after 2 p.m. Friday, March 27, on Beach Road, close to Woods’ home. Deputies arrived on the scene to find one vehicle on its side. Authorities say Woods, who was driving a Land Rover alone, attempted to pass a truck before the crash while driving at a high rate of speed.The area where the crash happened, on Beach Road in Jupiter Island, Florida. — Google Maps street viewNBC affiliate WPTV, Channel 5 in West Palm Beach, reported that no injuries were sustained in the two-vehicle accident. However, Woods was taken into custody shortly after the crash and has been charged with driving under the influence.At a news conference, Martin County Sheriff’s Office officials said Woods passed a breathalyzer test with a result of triple zeros, indicating no alcohol in his system.However, he refused to submit to a legally required urine test at the jail, leading to an additional charge for refusal to consent to a lawful test. Under local law, he must be held for a minimum of eight hours. He was also charged with property damage.Jupiter Island, Florida (marked in red), is located just north of West Palm Beach. — Google MapsWoods' history of previous crashes is as follows:In February 2021, he was seriously injured in a single-vehicle rollover crash in Rancho Palos Verdes, California. Speeding was determined to be the cause. He suffered severe \"open fractures\" to his right tibia and fibula bones, as well as significant injuries to his right foot and ankle.In May 2017, Woods was arrested in Jupiter for DUI after being found asleep in his running car. A toxicology report revealed a mix of prescription drugs and THC in his system.In November 2009, Woods crashed his Cadillac Escalade into a fire hydrant and a tree outside his Windermere, Florida, home. The incident ultimately exposed his extramarital affairs to the public.Friday’s crash comes just days after Woods competed in the TGL Finals on Tuesday, March 24, representing Jupiter Links GC. It was his first competitive appearance in over a year following multiple surgeries, including a disc replacement last October. Observers noted he appeared to move better than he had in years.Woods had recently registered for the 2026 US Senior Open in July, but had not confirmed his participation. His status for the Masters next month remains unclear.Woods' girlfriend is 48-year-old Vanessa Trump, the ex-wife of Donald Trump Jr.President Donald Trump spoke about Woods' crash late Friday afternoon to reporters before boarding Air Force One.\"I feel so badly,\" Trump said. \"He's had some difficulty. There was an accident. That's all I know. He's a very close friend of mine. He's an amazing person, an amazing man, but some difficulty.\"Check back with Daily Voice for updates.",
